            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for a royal court, then the Arabic for to take office."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: فارس",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فارس — fāris — \"a knight, a horseman\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ركب الفارس حصانه الأبيض. rakiba al-fāris ḥiṣānahu al-abyaḍ. The knight rode his white horse."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: فرسان, fursān."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فارس (fāris) الأحلام: Prince Charming."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فارس (fāris) is built on the native Arabic root f-r-s (Lane), the root of faras, a horse. Fāris is the man on the horse; furūsiyya is horsemanship and knighthood."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
