              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "هدنة — hudna — \"a truce\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وقع الطرفان هدنة لمدة شهر. waqqaʿa aṭ-ṭarafān hudna li-muddat shahr. The two sides signed a truce for a month."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "هدنة (hudna) is a native Arabic word built on the root h-d-n, recorded in hudna ʿalā dakhan, an illusory truce (Lane). The root is usually explained as \"to be still, to be quiet\": a time when the fighting is still."
            }
          ]
        },
